  "about": "Quote vectors for the pool program's swap_base_input path. Two readers must reproduce every one: the Jupiter SDK (tests/quote_vectors.rs) and the site's own quote, quoteOwnPool in frontend/src/lib/solana/cpswap/read.ts (jupiterSdkParity.test.ts). `out` is what the curve pays; `refusal` names the program error that refuses the swap, or is null. A ZeroAmountOut refusal has out 0: the site quotes 0 there and its builders refuse it as too small. `live` swaps read the snapshots in accounts/<pool>/, the same files the LiteSVM parity test (tests/parity.rs) runs on. The two `fee_paths token-0 copy` cases are what the deployed program paid in tests/fee_paths.rs, which checks them. Amounts are raw token units, as decimal strings.",
